# NVDA — Fundamental Research Report
**Analysis date: 2026-09-01 | Source: SEC EDGAR facts filed on or before 2026-09-01 | Currency: USD millions unless stated**

---

## 1. Executive Summary

NVDA's fundamentals as of 2026-09-01 describe a company in an extraordinary second derivative expansion, not a decelerating one. The most recent reported quarter (Q2 FY2027, ended 2026-07-26) delivered **$96.2B revenue, $72.1B gross profit, $63.7B operating income and $59.7B net income ($2.46 diluted EPS)** — more than **double** the year-ago quarter on every line. Trailing-twelve-month revenue is **$303.0B (+83.4% y/y)** with TTM net income of **$192.9B (+122.7% y/y)**.

Critically, the quarterly year-over-year growth rate has **re-accelerated** for four consecutive quarters: +62.5% → +73.2% → +85.2% → **+105.9%**. Sequential growth, however, has begun to edge lower (+21.9% → +19.5% → +19.8% → +17.9%), and **gross margin has printed essentially flat at ~75.0% for two straight quarters (74.93%, 74.97%)** — evidence that the margin-recovery tailwind (from the depressed 60.5% gross margin in Q1 FY2026) is now exhausted. Forward earnings growth must therefore come from volume/mix, not margin.

The balance sheet is fortress-grade: **$320.3B assets, $229.0B equity, 4.59x current ratio, 28.5% liabilities-to-assets**. But two items demand scrutiny: (a) **operating cash flow conversion collapsed to 63% of net income in H1 FY2027 (from 95% a year earlier)**, and (b) **$35.1B of investing outflow in H1 FY2027 (47% of operating cash flow)**, largely non-capex deployment into external investments. These are the two places where reported earnings quality could diverge from economic reality.

**Valuation and insider data are unavailable at this point-in-time vintage (see §2)**, so this report deliberately provides an earnings/multiple sensitivity matrix rather than asserting a multiple.

---

