**Data-quality flag (important):** The diluted EPS series is **not uniformly split-adjusted**. FY2022 EPS of $3.85 against net income of $9,752 implies ~2,533M shares (pre-10:1 split), while FY2023's $0.17 on $4,368 implies ~25,694M shares (post-split). The cutover is inconsistent even within FY2024 (2023-04-30 shows pre-split, 2024-04-28 shows post-split). **Use net income, not the historical EPS series, for any multi-year growth analysis.** All figures from Q3 FY2026 onward used in this report are internally consistent.

---

## 3. Company Profile (background context, not vendor-sourced)

NVDA is a **fabless semiconductor and accelerated-computing platform company**. It designs GPUs and system-scale accelerated computing platforms (chips, boards, full racks, networking via NVLink/InfiniBand/Ethernet, and systems), monetized through hardware plus the **CUDA software ecosystem** and enterprise AI software. Reporting segments historically span Data Center, Gaming, Professional Visualization, and Automotive — with **Data Center the overwhelming majority of revenue and effectively all of recent growth**. Manufacturing is outsourced to TSMC with advanced packaging (CoWoS) and high-bandwidth memory (HBM) from a small supplier set, making supply — not demand — the binding constraint in upcycles.

Business-model implications visible directly in the numbers: **asset-light (capex just 6% of operating cash flow in H1 FY2027), extremely high incremental margins, but highly exposed to a concentrated hyperscale/cloud customer base and to export-control policy.**

