*¹ Not comparable — split-adjustment inconsistency (see §2).*

**Three-year context:** Revenue compounded from $26,974M (FY2023) to $215,938M (FY2026) — **8.0x in three years (100% CAGR)**. Net income went from $4,368M to $120,067M — **27.5x**. Five-year revenue CAGR from FY2021 is **66.8%**.

**FY2023 is the single most instructive historical analog for risk management.** Revenue was essentially flat (+0.2%) yet net income fell 55.2% and gross margin compressed from 64.9% to 56.9% on inventory write-downs and a customer-inventory correction. **Flat top-line can still halve earnings in this business.** That is the shape of the bear case — not a demand collapse, but a gross-margin and inventory air-pocket.

Note also that **FY2026 gross margin (71.1%) declined ~390bp from FY2025's 75.0%** even as revenue grew 65%. The company is currently earning below its FY2025 peak margin despite 65% more revenue — evidence of rising HBM/package/system-content cost pressure, offset more recently by pricing and mix.

