The declining payout ratio is **not** a policy shift — it is net income outrunning the buyback authorization's pace. The dividend is nominal (~$0.01/quarter), so essentially all financing outflow is buyback.

**Share count (inferred from NI ÷ diluted EPS):**

| Period | Implied Diluted Shares (M) |
|---|---|
| FY2024 | 25,008 |
| FY2025 | 24,789 |
| FY2026 | 24,504 |
| Q2 FY2026 | 24,465 |
