| Q2 FY2027 | 24,263 |

Shares are shrinking **~1.0–1.2% per year despite heavy buybacks** — meaning **share-based compensation is consuming roughly three-quarters of the repurchase program's effect**. The true return of capital to shareholders is far smaller than the $48B financing outflow implies. Without an SBC line in the dataset this cannot be quantified precisely; request it if SBC-adjusted ("cash") EPS matters to your model.

