## 10. Valuation Framework (price data withheld — sensitivity matrix provided instead)

No price, market cap, or multiple is available at this vintage. Rather than assert a valuation, here is the earnings base you should apply your own multiple to:

- **TTM diluted EPS: $7.91**
- **Q2 FY2027 annualized run-rate EPS: ~$9.84** ($2.46 × 4) — the cleanest current earning power, since Q1 FY2027 contained ~$4.8B of non-operating gains
- **FY2027E (ending Jan 2027) constructive case:** If Q3/Q4 grow ~10% and ~10% sequentially (vs 17.9% in Q2), FY2027 revenue ≈ **$400B** and, at a 62% net margin, EPS ≈ **$10.2**
- **FY2028E:** +25% revenue growth with flat margins implies EPS ≈ $12.5–12.8

**Implied price matrix (illustrative only — plug in actual quote):**

| P/E applied | on TTM $7.91 | on Run-rate $9.84 | on FY27E $10.2 | on FY28E $12.6 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 20x | $158 | $197 | $204 | $252 |
| 25x | $198 | $246 | $255 | $315 |
| 30x | $237 | $295 | $306 | $378 |
| 35x | $277 | $344 | $357 | $441 |
| 40x | $316 | $394 | $408 | $504 |

**How to use this:** The fundamental case does not depend on multiple expansion — EPS is growing ~100% y/y. It depends on **whether the multiple is being applied to a durable or a cyclical EPS number**. At 25x run-rate EPS the stock would be cheap for a 100%-growth asset; at 40x TTM it would require the growth to persist through FY2028. Position sizing should reflect which of those two regimes the current quote implies. Also note the implied **P/B**: at any price above ~$190, P/B exceeds 20x — book value is not a useful valuation anchor here.

